    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d183">

                <pb facs="0239" n="147" xml:id="pg147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the President</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d183-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-02">2 November 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Most secret for the President only from Hull</p>
                <p>A message has been given me from the person highest in authority to be delivered
                    to you personally in extreme secrecy. The message promises to get in and help to
                    defeat the enemy.</p>
                <p>Remainder follows in another code.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d183-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d183-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d183-f1-content">
                <p>Sent by the United States Naval Attaché Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d183-f2" n="2" xml:id="d183-f2-content">
                <p>Hull wrote, in his <hi rendition="#italic">Memoirs</hi>, vol. <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p. 1311: “The information Stalin had given
                    me on his decision regarding Japan I regarded as so secret that I sent one-half
                    of it to the President over the Navy code and the other half over the Army
                    code.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
